messages:
marta: FYI Windows Electron sampleapp is throwing JSON.parse errors while streaming SSE. Happens when a single token gets split across chunk boundary.

marta: repro steps - run the sampleapp on Win10 (Electron), start a long response, check logs. I see fragments like:
```
{"choices":[{"delta":{"content":"Hel"}}]}
```
then next chunk:
```
{"choices":[{"delta":{"content":"lo"}}]}
```
But the client tries to parse the first fragment as a complete JSON and fails.

dev-bot: deploy-bot: new build 2026-03-23 15:12 rolled to sampleapp/stable :package:
tyler: Do we only see this on Electron/Windows or also in Chrome/Node?

marta: Only repro'd on Electron on Win so far. Browser Chrome seems fine. Node SDK tests also mostly fine but I haven't tried the Node sampleapp on Windows.

sam: Could be two things: (1) our SSE framing logic assumes events always end with "\n\n" and doesn't gracefully handle CRLF or chunked splits, (2) auth refresh/abort may cause an early chunk cut where we attempt to parse partial event.

lee: On Windows CRLF is common. If we split on "\n\n" only, a stream producing "\r\n\r\n" will produce a trailing "\r" in the fragment. Also TextDecoder streaming can break multibyte UTF-8 chars across chunks. Need to accumulate and only parse completed events.

marta: Minimal fix I tested locally (works):
```
let buffer = "";
res.body.on('data', (chunk) => {
  buffer += chunk.toString('utf8');
  // normalize CRLF to LF
  buffer = buffer.replace(/\r\n/g, '\n');
  const events = buffer.split('\n\n');
  buffer = events.pop(); // incomplete tail
  events.forEach(ev => handleEvent(ev));
});
res.body.on('end', () => {
  if (buffer.trim()) handleEvent(buffer);
});
```
This avoids attempting JSON.parse on partial payload.

tyler: Nice. Can we make the SDK provide a helper that does canonical SSE reassembly for all sampleapps? We should avoid duplicating fix across repo.

sam: Agreed. Also add a small abstraction around TextDecoder with streaming true/false handling to avoid broken multibyte sequences.

lee: Test cases to add: simulate chunk boundary in the middle of a multibyte char and in middle of an escaped JSON sequence (e.g., "\\uD83D"). Also simulate auth refresh that injects an extra small chunk.

marta: I'll open a PR for sampleapp changes and a companion PR in node-sdk with a helper: sse/reassembly.js and tests that run on CI matrix for windows-latest. PR will be linked here.

marta: PR 1428 opened: https://git.internal/redwood/sampleapp/pull/1428 (contains sampleapp fix + tests).

tyler: Can you also add a short doc blurb in devex/README about "robust SSE handling" so folks reusing sampleapps don't copy the bad pattern?

marta: Yup, adding a section and a code snippet.

sam: After PR merges let's backport to the electron quickstart template and bump SDK minor.

lee: :eyes: Can we add a flaky test guard to the flaky CI run if Windows simulation fails intermittently?

marta: Will do. Confirmed locally on Win10 VM the fix prevents JSON.parse errors. I'll add a note in the PR about the observed chunks.

tyler: Thanks! Assigning to devex to track follow-ups. :shipit:

